      "eliminated_obligations": [
        "Builds an explicit finite total/cube times two-v-limb wall catalogue at each fixed rank, independent of N/coarse mesh/buffer/fine atom count.",
        "Proves every form proper from its nonzero first-coordinate response, without deleting equality or inherited regions.",
        "Uses the actual original ordinary upper admission log dictionary and constructed cap error to locate each ideal-admitted/buffered-rejected history itself.",
        "Directly consumes rejection of the new physical buffered second/third policy and derives the wall event.",
        "Derives required length/positive entries/order from an actual target-deleted prime frontier in the second-action specialization."
      ],
      "remaining_premises": [
        "A fixed rank r>=3 (r>=4 for the direct third-policy corollary); no uniform J0 is supplied.",
        "N is a natural number greater than one for the literal logarithmic admission dictionary.",
        "The generic history version uses the genuine history length, positive entries and reverse order; the frontier corollary derives those from real carrier membership.",
        "hi/hb are the actual admission-change event to be covered, not a coverage or mass-estimate hypothesis.",
        "This catalogue covers cap-approximation admission loss, not all O/P parity-compiler crossing/changed events; no total mass or reserve bound is assumed or concluded."
      ]
